      "id": "now",
      "name": "Now",
      "category": "MonotonicTime",
      "signature": "Now()",
      "params": [],
      "returnType": "FMonotonicTimePoint",
      "docs": "A point in time measured in seconds since an arbitrary epoch.\nThis is a monotonic clock which means the current time will never decrease. This time is meant\nprimarily for measuring intervals. The interval between ticks of this clock is constant except\nfor the time that the system is suspended on certain platforms. The tick frequency will differ\nbetween platforms, and must not be used as a means of communicating time without communicating\nthe tick frequency together with the time."
